  "description": "SULPAR crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H64 Cl2 Dy4 N12 O18. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.737-3.883 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.46-114.84°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C64H66Cl2Dy4N12O18. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
